Read CURSOR_PROJECT_CONTEXT.md first, then the relevant docs/cursor-handoff chapter and current source. Evidence order: executable code, schema/migrations, tests, current docs, master context, handoff, historical comments.
Audit existing services/adapters before adding abstractions; do not create parallel sending, audience or automation systems.
Distinguish proof, real code and externally verified production behavior. Proof runtime can use real AWS when flags enable it.
Preserve tenant authorization, immutable published versions, protected suppression, durable inbox/outbox and unknown-submission safeguards.
Never copy credentials/signing secrets into prompts, docs, client env or logs. Do not run migrations, destructive data operations or AWS resource changes merely to inspect behavior.
Document source-backed conflicts and unknowns; passing tests/gates are not production certification.

